		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">29</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following are some hints for coming up with new test cases.

1. Normal test cases - length of the list is like 5, 8, 10 etc.
1.1 A mix of positive, negative and 0
1.2. All positive lifespans
1.3. All same lifespans

2. Boundary test cases
2.1. List contains multiple values, but all are negative
2.2. List contains multiple values, but all are 0
2.3. List contains multiple values, all are negative except one (which is positive)
2.4. List contains multiple values, all are negative except one (which is 0)
2.5. List contains only one value, which is positive
2.6. List contains only one value, which is negative
2.7. List contains only one value, which is 0

Based on these hints, you can come up with at least 10 new test cases.
Write them on a paper along with the expected output.</attribute>
